156191.0,"2022-23":166281.0,"2023-24":175983.0,"2024-25":186323.0},"prov":{"description":"Financing - COUNCIL TAX REQUIREMENT (TOTAL OF LINES 805 TO 885)","form":"RS","row":"890","col":"1"}},{"label":"Net revenue expenditure","code":"RS_netrevexp_net_exp","by_year":{"2017-18":226494.0,"2018-19":240932.0,"2019-20":250517.0,"2020-21":254724.0,"2021-22":273850.0,"2022-23":307052.0,"2023-24":340964.0,"2024-25":349952.0},"prov":{"description":"NET current expenditure - NET REVENUE EXPENDITURE (TOTAL OF LINES 800 TO 804)","form":"RS","row":"805","col":"1"}}]}],"context":[{"label":"Resident population","value":351592,"year":"2020 est.","kind":"int"},{"label":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":10250000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":28332,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":31580,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2296.89,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":1891.63,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Wakefield's 2025/26 treasury outturn was fully compliant: the CFR rose \u00a313.5m to \u00a3571.3m while external borrowing actually fell \u00a33.1m to \u00a3377.9m (PWLB \u00a3346.4m, other local authorities \u00a326.5m, banks \u00a35m), leaving the council \u00a3131.9m under-borrowed and running on internal cash \u2014 capital slippage saved \u00a34.2m of borrowing costs and the treasury budget underspent \u00a33.85m. The average rate paid on external debt was 4.80%, and the council flags that the LA-to-LA borrowing market is 'becoming tight' as other authorities chase the same borrow-short-until-rates-fall strategy; investments stood at \u00a357m (\u00a340m in the DMO deposit facility, \u00a317m lent to other councils). A legacy MRP overpayment that has been suppressing the revenue charge for debt is nearly exhausted \u2014 \u00a35.3m left, fully used by end-2026/27, after which all MRP hits the revenue budget. Financing costs ran at 11.30% of net revenue (9.68% excluding PFI) against budgets of 13.16% and 9.70%.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management for the year ending 31 March 2026.","as_of_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138268/TM Outturn Report 2025-26.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-29","signals":[{"code":"refinancing-risk","headline":"\u00a3131.9m under-borrowed against the \u00a3571.3m CFR at 31 March 2026, on a deliberate short-term debt stance, while the council itself reports the LA-to-LA borrowing market 'becoming tight'","why":"The deferred borrowing need must eventually be financed externally, and the council's preferred market for short money is the one it says is tightening."},{"code":"debt-servicing-rising","headline":"Legacy MRP overpayment offset down to \u00a35.3m at 31 March 2026 and fully utilised by end-2026/27 \u2014 thereafter all MRP is charged to the revenue budget; the average rate paid on external borrowing was already 4.80% in 2025/26","why":"A structural step-up in the revenue cost of debt arrives from 2027/28, just as deferred borrowing may need to be externalised at current rates."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3571.312m closing CFR, up \u00a313.5m in the year (including a \u00a34.917m IFRS16 opening adjustment); MRP charged \u00a311.858m","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":4},{"name":"external borrowing","value":"\u00a3377.9m \u2014 \u00a3346.4m PWLB, \u00a35m banks, \u00a326.5m local authorities \u2014 less \u00a310.3m of borrowing held on behalf of other local authorities","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":1},{"name":"internal borrowing","value":"\u00a3131.866m under-borrowing (total gross debt \u00a3439.447m including PFI \u00a365.346m and leases \u00a36.484m, vs CFR \u00a3571.312m)","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":6},{"name":"la borrowing short term","value":"\u00a326.50m borrowed from local authorities, down \u00a335.50m from \u00a362.00m a year earlier","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":8},{"name":"la lending","value":"\u00a317.00m invested with other local authorities, out of \u00a357.00m total treasury investments (\u00a340.00m in the Debt Management Account Deposit Facility, nil with banks)","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":9},{"name":"financing costs to net revenue","value":"11.30% including PFI and other financing arrangements vs 13.16% budget; 9.68% excluding PFI vs 9.70% budget","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":7},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"Net treasury revenue outturn \u00a319.904m vs \u00a323.754m budget \u2014 \u00a33.850m underspend","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":10},{"name":"average borrowing rate","value":"4.80% average rate of interest paid on external borrowing during 2025/26 (long-term debt taken 1982\u20132008 at 4.2%\u201311.5%, plus recent temporary borrowing at inflated rates)","page":8},{"name":"mrp overpayment balance","value":"\u00a35.3m legacy MRP overpayment remaining (from \u00a361.7m at 1 April 2017; \u00a37.2m used in 2025/26); fully utilised by end 2026/27, thereafter all MRP charged to the revenue budget","as_at":"2026-03-31","page":5},{"name":"capital expenditure","value":"\u00a380.388m capital spend in 2025/26, of which \u00a315.762m (19.6%) funded from prudential borrowing","page":3}],"commercial":null,"tms_components":null},"compliance":{"score":137,"max":213,"pct":64,"assessed":"2026-02-17","notes":"Strong, professionally advised (Link) combined capital + treasury strategy: prudential indicators, a 10-year liability benchmark, MRP policy, borrowing strategy and creditworthiness/counterparty policy are all well developed, and every applicable core requirement scores >=2. Weakest areas are the non-treasury/commercial-investment framework (no explicit paras 51-53 compliance statement, no confirmed IMPs, no monetary limits on service/commercial investment, thin statutory disclosures, guarantees not reassessed), the absence of a quantitative investment-portfolio risk indicator (INV-06), accounts-linked reporting items not evidenced in the strategy (audit-qualification flag, financial-instruments disclosures), and ESG which is only referenced as a future Code requirement. Note: the documents contain no HRA content (housing stock transferred to WDH), so HRA-split and separate-HRA-benchmark elements are treated as not applicable.","gaps":[{"id":"COM-02","evidence":"TMSS p.5 \u00a71.1.4-1.1.5 describes Prudential Code commercial-investment requirements incl no-borrow-for-yield"},{"id":"COM-05","evidence":"TMSS p.5 \u00a71.1.4 notes the requirement to 'create new investment management practices' for non-treasury investments"},{"id":"COM-07","evidence":"Cap Strat p.13 \u00a74.1.1-4.1.3 investment-property NBV \u00a386.2m & income-dependence ratio <1% with exposure-to-loss commentary"},{"id":"COM-09","evidence":"TMSS p.5 \u00a71.1.5 notes requirement for limits on service and commercial investments"},{"id":"COM-10","evidence":"Cap Strat p.13 \u00a74.1.3 commercial-income ratio reported; \u00a71.5 quarterly capital monitoring to Cabinet"},{"id":"INV-06","evidence":""}],"documents":[{"title":"Capital, Investment and Treasury Management Strategy 2026/27 (Cabinet report)","url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s136555/Report%20-%20Capital%20Investment%20and%20Treasury%20Management%20Strategy%202026-27.pdf","fy":"2026/27"},{"title":"Appendix 1 - Capital and Investment Strategy 2026/27","url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s136556/Appendix%201%20Capital%20and%20Investment%20Strategy%202026-27.pdf","fy":"2026/27"},{"title":"Appendix 3 - Treasury Management Strategy Statement 2026/27 (incl. MRP Policy & Annual Investment Strategy)","url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s136558/Appendix%203%20Treasury%20Management%20Strategy%20Statement%2026-27.pdf","fy":"2026/27"},{"title":"Appendix 4 - Treasury Management Mid-Year Report 2025/26","url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s136559/Appendix%204%20TM%20Mid-Year%20Report%20202526.pdf","fy":"2025/26"}]},"documents