026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix 12 - OS Budget Response 2026-27","url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk/documents/s136782/appendix-12-os-budget-response-2026-27.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"02/03/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[{"title":"Treasury Management for the year ending 31 March 2026.","url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138268/TM Outturn Report 2025-26.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"2026-07-29","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Regeneration and Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10:00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-12","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10:00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Council","time":"2:00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5:30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Children and Young People Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10:00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Corporate and Resources Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10:00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-17","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5:30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-19","committee":"Adult Services and Health Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"2:00 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Children and Young People Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10:00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Adult Services and Health Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"2:00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Ethics and Governance Committee","time":"2:00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Corporate and Resources Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10:00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5:30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://mg.wakefield.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Wakefield cuts capital programme by \u00a356m as spending lags and oversight remains incomplete","lead":"Wakefield Council has reduced its five-year capital programme from \u00a3414.7m to \u00a3358.5m in the first quarter of 2026-27, with a further reprofiling planned within weeks. Capital spending in the first three months reached only \u00a322m against a projected \u00a3138m quarterly rate, running at 15.9 per cent of profile. The revised programme relies on \u00a3140.2m of prudential borrowing (borrowing to fund long-lived assets), representing 39 per cent of total spending, but the council has provided no detailed assessment of how this will affect the revenue budget. The Cabinet papers acknowledge that governance arrangements for the capital programme are currently under review and do not yet fully embed the Duty of Best Value. A further reprofile and budget challenge will take place in the second quarter.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - treasury indicators q1","paper_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138848/138848.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"22.09.26 10 point briefing Cabinet Report Disposal Programme","paper_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138856/138856.pdf","headline":"Governance changes remove barriers to property disposals, suggesting previous delays and new urgency.","detail":"The Scheme of Delegation is being amended to restrict ward members' ability to block or pause disposals. Previously any ward member objection could halt a disposal; the new approach allows objections only on 'legitimate grounds' for retention or alternatives. This suggests ward opposition has previously delayed key disposals.","category":"governance","matters":"It shows the council recognises disposal pace is critical to meeting budget targets and has removed a governance bottleneck, increasing credibility of programme delivery.","figures":"None","quote":"the Leader will amend the Scheme of Delegation to only permit such objections where legitimate grounds exist to support retention or an alternative to disposal","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"22.09.26 10 point briefing Cabinet Report Disposal Programme","paper_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138856/138856.pdf","headline":"Property disposal programme is explicitly tied to meeting the council's essential revenue budget savings.","detail":"The council's Property, Facilities, Health & Safety service is using the disposal programme to meet essential revenue budget savings by reducing holding costs and generating capital receipts. This signals the council faces material property costs that are part of its budget challenge.","category":"savings","matters":"A lender needs to understand councils' strategies for addressing budget pressures; identifying property costs as controllable allows assessment of the council's financial management approach and available levers.","figures":"No specific savings targets or capital receipt amounts provided.","quote":"This will allow the Council's Property, Facilities, Health & Safety service (PFHS) to meet essential revenue budget savings by reducing holding costs and generating capital receipts","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 point briefing - Capital","paper_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138858/138858.pdf","headline":"Prudential borrowing requirement of \u00a3140.2m over five years to deliver \u00a3358.5m capital programme","detail":"The capital programme requires \u00a3140.2m of prudential borrowing over five years. The council's total gross borrowing at 30 June stood at \u00a3340m, comprising \u00a3333m from PWLB and \u00a37m from inter-authority lending.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Shows the scale of additional borrowing committed and confirms funding is arranged through low-cost PWLB sources","figures":"\u00a3140.2m prudential borrowing; \u00a3358.5m total capital programme; \u00a3340m total gross borrowing","quote":"The revised capital programme requires \u00a3140.2m of prudential borrowing over the 5 years.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 point briefing - Capital","paper_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138858/138858.pdf","headline":"Capital spending in first quarter at only 15.9% of the annual \u00a3138m target, with further review planned","detail":"Of the \u00a3138m planned for 2026/27, only 15.9% was spent in the first quarter. The council acknowledges this slow delivery and states that review and challenge of planned spending will be undertaken in the next quarter.","category":"capital","matters":"Slower-than-expected capital delivery in early quarter indicates potential project delay risk that could affect funding drawdown timing and borrowing requirements","figures":"15.9% of \u00a3138m","quote":"Of the \u00a3138m planned spend in 2026/27 only 15.9% was spent in the first quarter.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 point briefing_Highways Asset Management Funding_","paper_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138851/138851.pdf","headline":"Council has secured \u00a32,522,818 of additional CRSTS uplift funding from the Department for Transport for highways asset management in 2026/27.","detail":"This uplift funding from the West Yorkshire Combined Authority supplements the baseline CRSTS allocation for highways asset maintenance and improvements across the district. The funding supports the Council's statutory duty to maintain public highways under Section 41 of the Highways Act 1980. Cabinet is asked to accept the funding and approve its inclusion in the Council's Capital Programme.","category":"capital","matters":"Securing additional external capital funding beyond baseline allocations strengthens the council's financial position by reducing reliance on borrowing and demonstrates successful access to grant funding from higher-tier authorities.","figures":"\u00a32,522,818","quote":"The Council has secured \u00a32,522,818 of additional capital funding from the Department for Transport via WYCA for highway asset management and maintenance during 2026/27.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-22"},"name":"Wakefield","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"Governance changes remove barriers to property disposals, suggesting previous delays and new urgency.","lead":"It shows the council recognises disposal pace is critical to meeting budget targets and has removed a governance bottleneck, increasing credibility of programme delivery.","also":["20 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Regeneration and Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-10-01","n_findings":21,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"22.09.26 10 point briefing Cabinet Report Disposal Programme","top_paper_url":"https://wakefield.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s138856/138856.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":90,"news_drafts_total":1}}